Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: tegra194: match nvethernet EQOS FIFO depths

NVIDIA's Tegra194 nvethernet v5.0 policy uses 9 KiB RX FIFO per
active queue. Its TX policy derives queue depth from a 36 KiB total
FIFO, which also yields 9 KiB per queue with the four active TX
queues used by this configuration.

stmmac otherwise uses the hardware-reported 64 KiB RX/TX FIFO sizes
and divides them across the configured queues, producing 16 KiB per
queue. Override the total FIFO depths to 36 KiB so the four-queue
mainline configuration matches NVIDIA's 9 KiB-per-queue policy in
both directions.

This only changes Tegra194 EQOS device-tree policy; other stmmac
platforms are unaffected.

Target: Linux 6.18.46 after the pinned reference and local PBL patches.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local hardware-validated tuning policy]

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra194.dtsi
@@ -175,6 +175,8 @@ ethernet@2490000 {
 			/* Match NVIDIA nvethernet's Tegra194 EQOS PBL programming. */
 			snps,txpbl = <32>;
 			snps,rxpbl = <12>;
+			tx-fifo-depth = <36864>;
+			rx-fifo-depth = <36864>;
 			snps,mtl-rx-config = <&eqos_mtl_rx_setup>;
 			snps,mtl-tx-config = <&eqos_mtl_tx_setup>;
